## Sign-in

::::row[icon=login href=# trailing-label="Manage" trailing-action=managePasskeys]
Passkeys
2 enrolled · primary sign-in
::::

::::row[icon=doc action=toggleEmailCodes href=# trailing-label="On" trailing-action=toggleEmailCodes]
Email codes — ON
Fallback sign-in toggle
::::

Email codes stay ON as the fallback when no passkey is available. The toggle renders as a row with the ON state in the title (toggle-switch treatment deferred with the notifications preferences); the current field value rides in the profile form's placeholder — prefill is state layer.

## About

::::row[icon=doc href=#]
Surfspace
Web · surf.space · Privacy Policy · Terms of Use
::::

::::row[icon=file style=danger action=openDeleteAccount href=#]
Delete account
Permanent — requires password + typed confirmation
::::

:::

::

Sign out lives here (Account group, danger row with the signed-in email) — moved OUT of the hub sheet per the 08-03 ruling. The title row is circled back + title only — no actions to convert (G3 pass, WP-N3 08-11). At small width (≤ 767px, R-C ruling 08-10) the shell contract applies unchanged: the sidebar hides behind the generated tab-bar + FAB, the 880px column goes full-width with edge padding, and the rows, forms, and trailing Change/Manage actions flow full-width and stay visible at touch widths.

## Sheets — defined once, opened from here

- **Delete account** — `modals/delete-account.surf` (`name=delete-account`), via the danger row (`openDeleteAccount`): consequence statement, password + typed-phrase confirmation gating the danger button.
- **Passkeys** — `modals/passkeys.surf` (`name=passkeys`), via Manage (`managePasskeys`): credential rows with trailing actions.
- **Notification preferences** — the Notifications row (`openNotificationPrefs`) routes to the preferences pane in `surfaces/notifications.surf`.
